# Springhill Medical Center — Enterprise Network Deployment

## Project Overview
This academic group capstone project involved designing and deploying a simulated enterprise network for Springhill Medical Center, a multi-tenant medical facility.

The project was completed by a team of four students as part of Fanshawe College's Computer Systems Technician (CTN) program.

## Technologies Used
- Cisco IOS
- VLANs and Inter-VLAN Routing
- OSPF
- IPv4 and IPv6
- First Hop Redundancy Protocol (FHRP)
- Access Control Lists (ACLs)
- Windows Server
- Active Directory and Group Policy
- DNS and DHCP

## Project Highlights
- Designed a segmented network supporting 18 VLANs.
- Configured dynamic routing and backup static routes.
- Implemented network security using ACLs and switch port hardening.
- Configured Windows Server services and Group Policy.
- Performed connectivity, security, and failover testing.

